 "reading": "The held-out caps do not separate interpolation from extrapolation over this range. At caps 28, 64, 96, between fitted caps, the frozen shared curve has RMSE 0.0139 (max 0.0237) over 9 cells, inside its own leave-one-cell-out scale of 0.0193. At cap 128, one step above the fitted range, the RMSE is 0.0142 (max 0.0223) over 3 cells, against 0.0139 interpolated, so one step beyond the fit does not degrade measurably. The candidate-size offset is comparable (0.0151 interpolated, 0.0131 at cap 128). Two bounds apply. Cap 128 sits at 84% of current-16's saturation cap (152) and 80% of fresh-16's (160), and the 16-tag cells at 96 and 128 already fall below the curve (fresh -0.024 at 96, current -0.022 at 128), which is flattening near the ceiling rather than a curve that keeps rising; the fit is not admissible past those caps.",
 "block_reading": "The block holdout shows where the offset model can and cannot stand in for the block label. Holding out current-16 or fresh-16 leaves two blocks whose candidate sizes bracket the held-out one, and the curve plus size offset interpolates them at RMSE 0.0216 and 0.0197 against its own held-out scale of 0.0193. Holding out larger-28 leaves only the two 16-tag blocks, whose log candidate sizes differ by 0.0026; the fitted size coefficient is -5.17 against an intercept of 21.89 and predicts a coverage of -4.33, so that direction is not identified, and its RMSE is a rank-deficiency artifact rather than an extrapolation error.",
